Sure. All you have to do is edit the file defaults.nh, which is in the 
folder you installed Nethack to. Despite the .nh extention, it's just 
a test file, so you can open it with notepad. You can make backup copy 
first if you want, just to be safe. For full details on all the 
options, refer to Guidebook.txt, which is in the same folder.

> and maybe for wizmode too?

Probably the easiest way is to make a copy of your nethack shortcut 
then edit it (right-click, properties) to add -uwizard -D to the 
"Target". For example it might look like:
"C:\Program Files\Nethack\NetHackW.exe" -uwizard -D

Then you can use that shortcut whenever you want to play in wizard mode.

